		<outline text="Driving music sales through podcasting">
			<outline text="Two thoughts about driving music sales through mashups and hittests">
				<outline text=" Patrick Seemann 	

pse@patom.ch &lt;mailto:pse@patom.ch&gt; to adam
	 More options	  6:35 am (9 hours ago)
Hi Adam,


I just want to add two thoughts to the topic:


a) I listen to DSC on my commute which means that even when I
like the music from mashups and hittests (and this happens often
enough) I can't buy it right away. Back at home I usually don't
know the title/artist anymore and don't have the time to
relisten to DSC either. Would it be possible to list the songs
used in the masups/hittests directly in the show notes?


b) The best source to get mashup/hittest impact on music sales
would be Apple/ITMS. Can't you use your contacts inside Apple to
find out whether the sales number for a given title raises after
it has been played in DSC?


Kind regards,
Patrick"/>
				</outline>
			<outline text="Winwood on the HitTest - all your fault!">
				<outline text="Jason Hollowed 	

ben_nushmut@mac.com &lt;mailto:ben_nushmut@mac.com&gt; to adam
	 More options	  3:37 am (12 hours ago)
Hey Adam,


Just wanted to continue with the back-catalog line you brought up in DSC#230.  I actually have the Winwood album Back in the High Life from iTunes already, but I was inspired to listen to it again after nearly a year away from it.  OH MY GOD, I'm still amazed at how incredible Steve's voice was here.
And as brilliant as Higher Love is, my personal connection goes straight to the title track.  When I was born (October 28, 1986), that was the song playing on the radio when my dad got to see me for the first time.  Even though I was I newborn at that moment, the song still resonates with me and actually brought me to tears in my dorm room as I listened to it (I was alone, but it wouldn't have mattered if I heard it with one or a dozen people in my room.  It just reaches deep into my soul and brings out a part of me I'm still amazed even exists.


Anyway, just wanted to thank you for a great podcast, I only wish I had the kind of time and resources you have to devote to your show to give to my podcast that I just started (yes, this is a plug coming in for landing!).


It's about the college experience on a campus in (literally) the middle of nowhere, Missouri.  The first episode was a soundseeing tour of my campus, the second features some clips from a concert I went to featuring a cover band.  Check it out if you have 45 mins for the first 2 shows.  It's at TruCast and in iTunes; search for TruCast.


Thanks and keep up the great work!  You are one of the reasons I've started doing my show!


Jason Hollowed
College Freshman, rookie podcaster, and (if all goes well) Future Music Educator
"/>
				</outline>
