kd7swh@gmail.com &lt;mailto:kd7swh@gmail.com&gt; to adam
	 More options	  Aug 28 (2 days ago)
Hi Adam,


Just wanted to let you know I have been here since day one of
iPodder.org, and will be a lifetime subscriber of the Source Code. Now
attending the University of Montana, (Missoula, Montana USA) I
volenteered as a technology assistant in my dorm so whenever I go out
on a call I tell the residents about  podcasting and RSS feeds. It
really seems to catch on quickly and everyone is joining &quot;the march&quot;.


As a side note in reference to your question about mash-ups in episode
229, I have bought at least ten CD's (AAC's worth) as a result of the
daily source code. Podcasts can also be great marketing tools if you
aren't afraid to put in the effort. If anyone needs an example, look
at Rob Costlow. I gave him his first Amazon.com review after hearing
him on the show and his amazon sales have surely gone up.


In any event, there is no question that &quot;we&quot; can make it (&quot;the march&quot;) happen.


Best Regards,


Jon Pieleat (Pie-lay)
Miller Hall at the University of Montana-Missoula"/>
