			<outline text="From a dad">
				<outline text=" Ben Collins 	
to adam
	 More options	  12:05 am (16 hours ago)
This past weekend I introduced my son Nick, (13) to the concept of a podcast.  We listened to a few that I subscribe to and spent some time talking about what he could do one on.  Nick is pretty typically into what most 13 year old boys are, particular video games which he will play as many hours as he can stay awake.  He's pretty computer literate and in about half an hour I showed him the basics of Sound Forge and Acid. 


He sat and worked for about 4 hours straight and designed and created his own podcast; gameSNAFU.  At the end of the day he was thrilled with his own efforts and success. For a teenager that is phenomenal concentration and follow through.  He spent the rest of the day IM-ing his friends planning new episodes and working on his subscriber base.  Wow.


As every teenager will tell you, they are smart and insightful.  And as any parent will tell you, they need focus, guidance and a creative outlet.  Podcasting fits the bill brilliantly.  It can be simple or technically sophisticated, meaningful or silly...whatever they want.  And it gives them something to do that is active not passive at a time in life when that is really important.


Many thanks,
Ben Collins
"/>
				</outline>
